    {
      "id": "behringer-px3000",
      "manufacturer": "Behringer",
      "model": "Ultrapatch Pro PX3000",
      "category": "patchbay",
      "dimensions": {
        "widthMM": 482.6,
        "heightMM": 44.5,
        "depthMM": 93
      },
      "rackUnits": 1,
      "weightKG": 1.81,
      "notes": "48-point passive balanced TRS patchbay: 96 1/4\" TRS jacks as 48 rear and 48 front, giving 24 channels. Each channel runs rear row A (source in) to rear row B (destination out). The mode is set per channel by a switch on the top panel, so it has to be reached before the bay is racked under something: NORMAL breaks the rear link when either front jack is used, HALF NORMAL only when the lower front jack is, and THRU ties each rear jack straight to the front jack above it with no normal. Front row A is the upper row and taps or breaks the source, so it patches as a send; front row B is the lower row and feeds the destination, so it patches as a return. Passive, no power. Jacks and modes from Behringer's product page; the dimensions and weight are dealer figures, as Behringer's page does not give them.",
